                            {
                                "example_id": "a37eb1b5-c28e-47ce-9198-69e871ade359",
                                "sense_id": "88b35f60-21ef-3960-9348-633ff0dedb8d",
                                "text": "The nib, coarse or finely ground, is mixed with the sugar in a kind of edgerunner or grinding-mixer, called a melangeur. This consists of two heavy millstones supported on a granite floor."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "24af66ec-3fac-46f9-90d1-8e69493e0451",
                                "sense_id": "88b35f60-21ef-3960-9348-633ff0dedb8d",
                                "text": "The melangeur Mabel and I had set up two days ago to grind the beans and sugar together was still churning away. I peeked into the grinder. Surprisingly, the mixture had turned into a silky smooth liquid. “That's the chocolate liquor,”[…]"
